      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the probability that the number on the card is both a prime number and a multiple of 7, we first need to identify the prime numbers that are multiples of 7 within the range of 1 to 50. The only number that satisfies these conditions is 7 (since 7 is the only prime number that is a multiple of 7).\n\nTo calculate the probability, we need to count the total number of successful outcomes (drawing the card with a prime number that is a multiple of 7) and divide it by the total number of possible outcomes (which is 50, as there are 50 cards numbered 1 to 50 in the box).\n\nThe successful outcome in this case is 1 (for the card with the number 7), while the total number of possible outcomes is 50 (since there are 50 cards numbered 1 to 50).\n\nTherefore, the probability (p) is given by the ratio of successful outcomes to total outcomes:\n$$\n\\begin{align\\*}\np &= \\frac{\\text{\"successful outcomes\"}}{\\text{\"total outcomes\"}}\\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{50}\\\\\n\\end{align\\*}\n$$\n\nThe final answer is $\\boxed{\\frac{1}{50}}$.",
